  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 148 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nUpper flow pattern supports northwest flow tonight through late \nWednesday, with H5 flow turning more northerly heading into \nThursday. A weak shortwave traverses the flow this evening and \novernight, with a chance for light rain ahead of an approaching cold \nfront. Cooler air works into the Northern Plains and Upper Midwest \nWednesday into Thursday, bringing temperatures back into the range \nof normal for early to mid November. Daytime highs will be in the \n30s to low 40s Wednesday and in the 30s on Thursday and Friday. \nOvernight lows fall into the teens Thursday night into Friday \nmorning. Aside from a few scattered rain showers today, dry weather \nis expected to persist through much of the forecast period. \n\nLooking down the road a bit, there is growing support for a \npotentially active period of weather as we head into the second half \nof November. This starts with a strong signal for blocking across \nthe central CONUS and into most of the Canadian Prairies. Resultant \ntroughs form on either side of the H5 ridge, which eventually \ndislodge and work eastward. Ensemble clusters are beginning to \nsupport solutions that hint at precipitation toward the very end of \nthe forecast period.",
